{
  "vcon": "0.4.0",
  "uuid": "f8754b64-e643-8f69-8acb-d313f04c150b",
  "created_at": "2026-02-04T13:47:45-05:00",
  "subject": "Inbound call, Public Works",
  "parties": [
    {
      "name": "Carlos Rocha",
      "role": "resident",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    },
    {
      "name": "Kevin Sousa",
      "role": "clerk",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    }
  ],
  "dialog": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-04T13:45:03-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Public Works, this is Kevin. Good afternoon, how can I help?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-04T13:45:08-05:00",
      "duration": 13,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yes, hello, good afternoon. I am calling about the storm drain in front of my house. It is not working good. It is, how do you say, grunting. Very slow, and then the water comes back up."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-04T13:45:21-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay, a slow drain that backs up. Can I get the address?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-04T13:45:26-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "One hundred nine Ruggles Avenue. Up in Historic Hill."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-04T13:45:30-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "One-oh-nine Ruggles. Got it. And is this from a storm, or is it just, you know, regular weather?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-04T13:45:37-05:00",
      "duration": 17,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "No storm. Nothing now, the weather is dry. But any time we have a thaw, the snow melts a little, and the water goes to the drain and it backs up in the street. It stays there. I am worried it will go to my property."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-04T13:45:54-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yeah, that makes sense with the melt. Has it been doing this a while?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-04T13:46:00-05:00",
      "duration": 14,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yes, a while. This week again. I went out myself and I take the leaves off the grate with my hands. Wet leaves, very heavy. It helped, but only for ten minutes. Maybe ten. Then the same thing."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-04T13:46:14-05:00",
      "duration": 14,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "So the grate's clear but it's still slow, which tells me something's probably blocked further down. Okay, let me note this. Drain at one-oh-nine Ruggles, slow, backs up on thaw, resident cleared the grate by hand, temporary relief only."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-04T13:46:28-05:00",
      "duration": 2,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yes, correct, exactly this."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-04T13:46:30-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "And I've got a number for you, is it still the same one, four-oh-one, five-five-five, oh-one-nine-six?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-04T13:46:36-05:00",
      "duration": 3,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yes, that is the number. Oh-one-nine-six, yes."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-04T13:46:39-05:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Please, can I ask. You will open a work order? And for what date? I want to understand when somebody comes."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-04T13:46:47-05:00",
      "duration": 17,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I'll put in the work order right now, so that part's done when we hang up. The date I can't give you exactly, because the crew supervisor sets the schedule. Drains that are backing up like this usually get looked at sooner than routine ones, though."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-04T13:47:04-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "So the order is open today, but the date, I do not know yet. I understand correct?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-04T13:47:11-05:00",
      "duration": 11,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "That's right. Opened today, date to be scheduled by the crew. If it gets worse, or water's heading toward your house, call us back right away and we'll bump it up."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-04T13:47:22-05:00",
      "duration": 11,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay, okay. Thank you. I am home all day, because I am working in the garage. I am rebuilding an engine of a lawn mower, only for the fun."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-04T13:47:33-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Nice, good project for a cold day. Alright, Mr. Rocha, you're all set on our end."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-04T13:47:39-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Thank you very much, Kevin. Have a good afternoon."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-04T13:47:43-05:00",
      "duration": 2,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "You too. Take care."
    }
  ],
